      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        Core Model Specifications &amp; Dimensional Architecture: 1024 vs 3072 Dimensions
      </h2>
      <p>
        Dense embedding models represent the mathematical backbone of modern semantic search, retrieval-augmented generation (RAG), and zero-shot clustering systems. While both Cohere Embed v3 (specifically <code>embed-english-v3.0</code>) and OpenAI <code>text-embedding-3-large</code> represent the current state of the art in commercial embedding APIs, they embody fundamentally divergent architectural philosophies regarding dimensionality, context size, and compression trade-offs.
      </p>
      <p>
        OpenAI generates high-dimensional representations by default: <strong>3,072 dimensions in single-precision floating point (float32)</strong>. While higher dimensionality offers expansive hyper-dimensional capacity for subtle conceptual nuances, it carries an immense penalty in downstream database RAM and disk I/O. Cohere caps its flagship model at <strong>1,024 dimensions</strong>, relying on proprietary contrastive fine-tuning and asymmetric projection layers to pack equivalent semantic density into one-third of the vector space.
      </p>

