              <td class="p-3">Fixed 1024 (or compress to int8/binary)</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-emerald-400 font-bold">Matryoshka (256, 512, 1024, 3072)</td>
              <td class="p-3 text-emerald-300">OpenAI flexible dimension slicing</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>

      <p>
        The context window disparity represents an important architectural dividing line. Cohere's 512-token ceiling strictly enforces dense chunking strategies (such as 400-word sliding windows with 50-word overlaps). This is generally considered best practice in enterprise retrieval to avoid semantic dilution. In contrast, OpenAI's 8,191-token context enables entire documents, contracts, or long forum threads to be encoded in a single call, although our empirical evaluations demonstrate that embedding chunks larger than 1,000 tokens results in a measurable degradation of specific factual recall.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white border-b border-slate-800 pb-2">
        MTEB &amp; BEIR Benchmark Suite: Empirical Retrieval Accuracy Metrics
      </h2>
      <p>
        To evaluate real-world information retrieval quality beyond marketing claims, we tested both models across the authoritative <strong>Massive Text Embedding Benchmark (MTEB)</strong> and domain-specific subsets of the <strong>BEIR (Benchmarking Information Retrieval)</strong> suite. Measurements were conducted across 8 diverse evaluation tasks spanning technical question answering, financial tabular retrieval, biomedical papers, and legal case law.
      </p>

